# Evolution Policy

Spec: EvolutionPolicy
Purpose:
  Define approval levels for system evolution. AI may detect
  potential knowledge evolution, but must NEVER silently change
  core rules, architecture, or policies. Every evolution must
  pass through the appropriate approval gate.

Owns: policies/evolution.sdd

ApprovalLevels:
  AUTO:
    changes:
      - add reference link
      - update usage counter
      - create task relationship
    rule: AI may execute without approval

  ASSISTED:
    changes:
      - create candidate skill
      - merge aliases
      - suggest concept
    rule: AI proposes; system validates

  REVIEW:
    changes:
      - architecture change
      - new global skill
      - change project rule
    rule: requires human review before promotion

  HUMAN_ONLY:
    changes:
      - security policy
      - production architecture
      - compliance rule
      - destructive migration
    rule: AI creates proposal only; human must approve

LevelAssignment:
  CONCEPT:            AUTO
  PROJECT_SKILL:      ASSISTED
  ARCHITECTURE:       REVIEW
  GLOBAL_RULE:        HUMAN_ONLY

  rule: AI must NOT auto-create canonical concepts from single observation

EvolutionBudget:
  max_new_concepts_per_task: 3
  max_new_skills_per_task: 1
  max_architecture_changes_per_task: 0

  rule: EVOLUTION_LIMIT_EXCEEDED → defer candidates, create knowledge review task

  KnowledgeExplosionProtection:
    if AI attempts: 1 task → 14 concepts → 9 skills → 4 rules → 3 architectures
    system: EVOLUTION_LIMIT_EXCEEDED
    action: defer candidates, create separate review task

CandidatePool:
  .sdd/evolution/
    ├── candidates/
    ├── challenges/
    ├── proposals/
    └── approved/

  Lifecycle: /tmp → /inbox → /candidates → /validated → /knowledge

InboxLifecycle:
  TMP     → ephemeral, may be deleted
  INBOX   → potentially valuable but unclassified
  CANDIDATES → proposed concepts awaiting validation
  VALIDATED   → confirmed by evidence
  KNOWLEDGE   → canonical, versioned, referenceable

State: +
